{"kind":"commit","url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/commit/6be4cd6560d17573f9ef9910bae4360cf96d760f","repo":"neovim/neovim","sha":"6be4cd6560d17573f9ef9910bae4360cf96d760f","set":"human","message":"refactor(charset)!: delete 'isprint' and cleanup 'iskeyword' and friends\n\nIn the `enc=utf-8` only world, the 'isprint' option is quite obsolete.\nThe function is only consulted for decoded U+0080 to U+00FF chars\nwhose printability is defined by the unicode charset, just like\nhigher codepoints. Meanwhile, invalid `\\x80` to `\\xFF` bytes are always\nunprintable.\n\nDisentangle 'iskeyword', 'isfname' and 'isident' from each other by\ngiving them all separate bitsets. Now these can be updated individually.\nThese updaters can back out of errors gracefully, no need for extra\npanic logic in option[str].c to restore partially updated chartabs.","files":[{"path":"runtime/doc/deprecated.txt","additions":1,"deletions":0},{"path":"runtime/doc/l10n-hebrew.txt","additions":0,"deletions":10},{"path":"runtime/doc/mbyte.txt","additions":1,"deletions":2},{"path":"runtime/doc/options.txt","additions":0,"deletions":30},{"path":"runtime/doc/pattern.txt","additions":2,"deletions":2},{"path":"runtime/doc/quickref.txt","additions":0,"deletions":1},{"path":"runtime/doc/usr_20.txt","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"runtime/doc/usr_27.txt","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"runtime/doc/various.txt","additions":1,"deletions":2},{"path":"runtime/doc/vimfn.txt","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"runtime/lua/vim/_meta/options.gen.lua","additions":0,"deletions":33},{"path":"runtime/lua/vim/_meta/vimfn.gen.lua","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/nvim/buffer.c","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/nvim/buffer_defs.h","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/nvim/charset.c","additions":53,"deletions":119},{"path":"src/nvim/eval.lua","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/nvim/help.c","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/nvim/option.c","additions":6,"deletions":11}